!. I will be reading two files ->  [rcon.txt and tdata.txt]
!. Contains log information when ever you execute this in *.log
!. rcon file contains only one row giving configuration details
!. there are 7 numerical entries and last is a file string = [car-car-bike.txt]
!. 1. rcon[0] alpha slope in MhZ per micro second [26.0000]
!. 2. rcon[1] Fs sampling frequency in KhZ [4500.0000]
!. 3. rcon[2] control program control 1  0 -1 -2 [1]
!. 4. rcon[3] synthetic data 0 or 1 [0]
!. 5. rcon[4] numberOfTgts [5]
!. 6. rcon[5] N number of samples in the phase sepctrum kMUSIC [180]
!. 7. rcon[6] kmax is the number of time A matrix is read from file car-car-bike.txt [10]
!. 8. rcon[7] numberOfTgts [5]
!. 9. rcon[8] samples for FFT [512]
!. 0. rcon[9] acquired ADC samples [512]
!. 1. rcon[10] a flag needed 225 samples [0]
!. 2. rcon[11] range gain [25.9436]
!. 3. rcon[12] amplitude threshold in double** sortCluster(..) [0.2000]
!. 4. rcon[13] number of real columns of matrix [8]
!. 5. rcon[14] maximum number blocks to be iterated [30]
!. if control is -2 only documentation is displayed and returned back
!. if control is 0 file name taken from rcon file car-car-bike.txt if -1 single stepping is performed
!. if control is 1 file name taken from rcon file car-car-bike.txt and output range is multiplied by Rgain 25.9436
!. if synthetic = 1 tdata.txt data is used and a file synth.txt is created for future use
!. tdata.txt is organised as a matrix each row describes the target
!. first entry normalised frequency 2nd signal strength 3rd DOA in degrees
!. number of rows are taken as number of targets
